From 078e489a4897c74f6003b48b86b8f8190b330d4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:54:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ssc): suspend source devices across system sleep

The SSC keeps sampling an open sensor while the system sleeps, so the
ADSP never power-collapses and the SoC stays out of its deep sleep
states. The kernel suspends other source hardware on its own, but not
this.

Give source devices suspend and resume hooks, called from HookSleep and
HookWake next to the target suspend and resume, which gamepad reordering
keeps using on its own. The SSC driver disables its sensors' reports
until wake. SUSPEND_TARGET_DEVICES_ON_SLEEP=0 keeps the target devices
across sleep, so clients see no disconnect. Resuming targets that were
never suspended no longer removes them.

Assisted-by: LLM
